[?2004hroot@0b9607726f92:/task# bcftools +contrast -h
[?2004lcontrast: invalid option -- 'h'

About: Runs a basic association test, per-site or in a region, and checks for novel alleles and
       genotypes in two groups of samples. Adds the following INFO annotations:
       - PASSOC  .. Fisher's exact test probability of genotypic association (REF vs non-REF allele)
       - FASSOC  .. proportion of non-REF allele in controls and cases
       - NASSOC  .. number of control-ref, control-alt, case-ref and case-alt alleles
       - NOVELAL .. lists samples with a novel allele not observed in the control group
       - NOVELGT .. lists samples with a novel genotype not observed in the control group
Usage: bcftools +contrast [Plugin Options]
Plugin options:
   -a, --annots LIST                List of annotations to output [PASSOC,FASSOC,NOVELAL]
   -0, --control-samples LIST|FILE  File or comma-separated list of control (background) samples
   -1, --case-samples LIST|FILE     File or comma-separated list of samples where novel allele or genotype is expected
   -e, --exclude EXPR               Exclude sites and samples for which the expression is true
   -f, --max-allele-freq NUM        Calculate enrichment of rare alleles. Floating point numbers between 0 and 1 are
                                        interpreted as ALT allele frequencies, integers as ALT allele counts
       --force-samples              Continue even if some samples listed in the -0,-1 files are missing from the VCF
   -i, --include EXPR               Include sites and samples for which the expression is true
   -o, --output FILE                Output file name [stdout]
   -O, --output-type u|b|v|z[0-9]   u/b: un/compressed BCF, v/z: un/compressed VCF, 0-9: compression level [v]
   -r, --regions REG                Restrict to comma-separated list of regions
   -R, --regions-file FILE          Restrict to regions listed in a file
       --regions-overlap 0|1|2      Include if POS in the region (0), record overlaps (1), variant overlaps (2) [1]
   -t, --targets REG                Similar to -r but streams rather than index-jumps
   -T, --targets-file FILE          Similar to -R but streams rather than index-jumps
       --targets-overlap 0|1|2      Include if POS in the region (0), record overlaps (1), variant overlaps (2) [0]
   -v, --verbosity INT              Verbosity level
   -W, --write-index[=FMT]          Automatically index the output files [off]

Example:
   # Test if any of the samples a,b is different from the samples c,d,e
   bcftools +contrast -0 c,d,e -1 a,b file.bcf

   # Same as above, but read samples from a file. In case of a name collision, the sample name
   # has precedence: the existence of a file with a list of samples is not checked unless no such
   # sample exists in the VCF. Use a full path (e.g. "./string" instead of "string") to avoid
   # name clashes
   bcftools +contrast -0 samples0.txt -1 samples1.txt file.bcf

   # The same as above but checks for enrichment of rare alleles, AF<0.001 in this example, in a region
   bcftools +contrast -r 20:1000-2000 -f 0.001 -0 samples0.txt -1 samples1.txt file.bcf

